nebula changelog

1.0.3 (WIP)
  - (No real code change) Drop support for C++11 and CUDA <9.2; add support for modern versions of CUDA.
  - Require C++17 and CUDA 11.0 or newer (CUDA 13 requires C++17).
  - Build for several GPU architectures by default (compute capability 7.5 to 12.0, plus PTX); configurable through CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES.
  - GPU: stop with an error message instead of hanging when kernels cannot run on the GPU.
  - Bundle cstool and the ENDF data, and build ELSEPA (downloaded at build time); CMake builds everything, including the Python environment with cstool and (optionally) material files.
  - Add the SEM tutorial and an automated test for it.

1.0.2 (2021-05-26)
  - Fix bug where only partial simulations were done when a low number of primaries are provided (GPU version).

1.0.1 (2021-02-16)
  - Add support for Windows (thanks Alexander Skorikov)
  - Support CUDA Toolkit 11 (thanks Alexander Skorikov)
  - Add upper energy bound to simulations

1.0.0 (2020-06-02)
  - Initial release
